// Tunnel Subsystem Documentation
//
// Overview:
// The tunnel subsystem enables teleportation between tunnel entrances and exits in the mission.
// The maximum number of tunnels per zone is defined in the map's map_config\init.hpp file (max_tunnels_per_zone parameter).
//
// Requirements:
// - Place at least max_tunnels_per_zone Land_InvisibleBarrier_F objects in the editor with variable names following the pattern: inTunnelTeleport_XX (e.g., inTunnelTeleport_0, inTunnelTeleport_1)
// - When placing the Land_InvisibleBarrier_F the hit box should be just above the players head to avoid getting stuck on Barrier
// - Place objective spawn point objects with variable names following the pattern: inTunnel_objective_XX (e.g., inTunnel_objective_0, inTunnel_objective_1)
// - Minimum 1 inTunnel_objective_XX per tunnel, no maximum limit
//
// How it works:
// - The subsystem automatically detects and caches these objects during initialization
// - Each tunnel entrance gets assigned a random available objective spawn point
// - Players can use "Enter Tunnel" actions to teleport to the assigned objective
// - "Exit Tunnel" actions allow returning to the original entrance